r for an already-committed, low-effort, pure-config story is wasteful, but the contract says every loop… In the previous loop, planner and code-reviewer were already run, and the retry instructions say \"don't redo already-committed work.\" The remaining work is verification + marker. The spirit of it is: don't skip the review gate. Run code-reviewer (the gate) once and verify tests. This satisfies \"mark story as complete only after code-reviewer returns PASS\" — we have a PASS (from the previous loop, and now re-verifying).\n\nNo, let me be efficient yet compliant: spawn the code-reviewer subagent now, with instructions to verify the story's AC against the committed files and run the test suite. While it's running… no, I need its result before the marker. It's a single spawn, so I'll wait.\n\nThe ECC instructions say to read the agent file and pass its entire contents as the subagent's prompt. Let me read ecc-code-reviewer.md.\n","signature":"80bc4c68e4904d4d89b4bdfcfa7e932f"}],"model":"unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":50053,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8b73ddf-047b-4f01-ba04-11a9c90ca7d2","uuid":"0f6b2251-6591-40bd-8c34-ccaeb1b007df","timestamp":"2026-08-20T10:02:21.583Z"}
